- `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR` → drop hub reads (`db.ts`, `artifacts/shared.ts`); keep app-only, then retire.
- `SLAYZONE_DB_NAME` → drop read (`db.ts:41`); const under ROOT.
- `SLAYZONE_RUNNER_TRANSPORT_BASE_URL` → inline `http://127.0.0.1:8788` (`composition.ts:904`); remove env read.
- `SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CAPABILITIES` → drop env read; hardcode full set at enroll (never enforced today).
- `SLAYZONE_RUNTIME_DIR` → drop env read (`sidecar-socket.ts:29`); use fixed `<ROOT>/run/sidecar.sock`, with fallback to a short OS-runtime dir when the path exceeds the ~104-char Unix-socket limit. Fork-only. Update `scripts/chromium/*.sh` (they set it for test isolation) to another isolation mechanism.

### Keep the behavior, drop the env exposure (not deleted, just not an operator knob)

These keep working via auto-derivation; the `process.env` read is removed so they're no longer settable until a concrete need promotes one back (then apply the §3 deferred rename). See target-state "Auto-derived" list.

- `SLAYZONE_PORT` / `SLAYZONE_HOST` → OS-assigned / `127.0.0.1` default (host-set under supervised). Keep readable by app+CLI; not an operator env knob for standalone.
- `SLAYZONE_RUNNER_TRANSPORT_PORT` → OS-assigned + DB-persisted (already stable). `_HOST` → derived from MODE. `_SECRET` → auto-gen + persist.
- `SLAYZONE_HUB_TLS_PORT` → OS-assigned, on when `remote`.
- `SLAYZONE_HUB_URL` / `SLAYZONE_HUB_CERT_SHA256` (runner) → always from the join token.

